# Audit mode

When Matt's request matches **audit intent**, load the matching skill before substantive work:

- **`/myauditandfix-v2`** or **audit your work** → `.cursor/skills/audit/SKILL.md` + `loop.md` **Solo audit loop** (one Grok; stamps push OK)
- **`/verify-plan-v2`** → `.cursor/skills/verify-plan/SKILL.md` + `loop.md` **Solo plan loop** (one Grok; does not stamp push)
- **`/verify-plan`** → `.cursor/skills/verify-plan/SKILL.md` + `.cursor/skills/audit/references/loop.md` (dual)
- **`/oracle-retro`** → `.cursor/skills/oracle-retro/SKILL.md` only
- **Everything else audit-intent** → `.cursor/skills/audit/SKILL.md` (+ dual `loop.md` when `/myauditandfix`)

## Trigger (intent, not exact wording)

Fire on: **audit**, **/myauditandfix-v2**, **audit your work**, **audit our work**, **audit this work**, **session audit**, **audit what you just did**, **assess**, **health check**, **review the system**, **coverage audit**, **what's broken in**, **sanity check on**, **findings on** — investigation and a report, not bare implementation.

**Solo loop (fix + push OK):** **/myauditandfix-v2** (`.cursor/commands/myauditandfix-v2.md`) and informal **audit your work** — one Grok 4.6 `ROLE=solo_audit` agent per `loop.md` Solo audit loop (default cap **8**; trailing `full` thorough; `quick` cap 4). **Dispatch:** `audit_solo` in `.cursor/dispatch-settings.yaml` (Cursor pin `cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh`, allow `high`; **Grok/Claude omit always**; never Composer; never k3 as adjudicator).

**Dual-critic loop (fix + push OK):** **/myauditandfix** (`.cursor/commands/myauditandfix.md`) — session track + fix authorized; pipeline in `loop.md` (default cap **3**; trailing `full` → 4; always-delta post-fix; empty-skip when both session critic children emit substituted sentinels). Also: **audit and fix**, **fix any issues** (with dual-audit context).

**Oracle retro:** **/oracle-retro** — oracle-retro skill only (Closure Summary §9).

**Verify plan (dual):** **/verify-plan** — verify-plan skill + `loop.md`; plan-doc fixes only; does not unlock `git push`.

**Verify plan (compact):** **/verify-plan-v2** — verify-plan skill + `loop.md` Solo plan loop; one Grok; plan-doc fixes only; does not unlock `git push`.

**Session audit:** invoking thread only — not repo-wide `git diff`. **`TRACK=session`**. Prepr prepare on code sessions (Night School 465). Dual dispatch: Cursor critics pin `composer-2.5`; confirm prefer `cursor-grok-4.6-high`; fix `cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh`; **Grok/Claude omit always**; never Composer; never k3 as adjudicator. Solo dispatch: `audit_solo` (above). **Bugbot:** default off.

Do **not** load audit skill for: **/oracle-retro**, **`/verify-plan`** / **`/verify-plan-v2`** (verify-plan skill), explicit **`/review-bugbot`**, or security-only review.

## Hard constraints

1. **Read-only by default** — fixes only when authorized (`/myauditandfix-v2`, `audit your work`, `/myauditandfix`, `/verify-plan` / `/verify-plan-v2` plan-docs, `/oracle-retro` encode, `and fix`, or `approved — build`)
2. **Assessment first** — **solo:** one Grok Task may audit+fix then re-audit in-loop; **dual:** dual critics + confirm (or empty-skip per `loop.md`); §4 before or with the loop payload; never confirm+write in one Task **on `/myauditandfix`** or **`/verify-plan`**; same-turn continue when slash loop not green
3. **Mandatory report sections** — Action summary → Verification ledger → Plan completion → Findings per audit skill §4 (`/oracle-retro` uses Closure Summary)
4. **Scope first** — one-line in/out before fan-out
5. **Delegate multi-area** — ≥2 independent areas → parallel Explore/Task
6. **Specialized tracks** — session/code/hybrid per audit skill; bugbot opt-in only
7. **Cursor product scope** → `cursor-guide` when auditing Cursor IDE/CLI behavior

## Precedence

Audit mode adds process on top of Fable + orchestration. It does **not** override workspace boundary, security floors, build gate, or orchestration case 1 (`cursor-guide`).
